---
import MetaBar from '@/components/MetaBar.astro';
import { legal, site } from '@/config/site';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = new Date(legal.privacyUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
});
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy" description="How smartargs processes personal data on smartargs.com.">
  <MetaBar>
    <span>Legal</span>
    <span>Updated {updated}</span>
  </MetaBar>

  <article class="px-5 pt-12 pb-16 sm:px-8 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-24">
    <h1 class="text-[length:clamp(3rem,7vw,6rem)] leading-[0.9] font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em]">
      Privacy policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-legal mt-12 max-w-2xl">
      <h2>Controller</h2>
      <p>The controller responsible for processing personal data on this website under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
      <address>
        {legal.name}<br />
        {legal.businessName && <>{legal.businessName}<br /></>}
        {legal.street}<br />
        {`${legal.postalCode} ${legal.city}`}<br />
        {legal.country}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>
      </address>

      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        We process personal data only where it is needed to run this website and to answer your requests. This website
        sets no cookies, shows no ads, uses no cross-site tracking, and serves its fonts from our own domain.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and delivery</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted and delivered by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you
        open a page, Cloudflare processes the technical data needed to deliver it and to protect the site from attacks:
        your IP address, the date and time of the request, the requested address, the referring page and your browser's
        user agent.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a secure and reliable website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare
        processes this data on our behalf under a data processing agreement. Cloudflare, Inc. is certified under the
        EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, for which the European Commission has adopted an adequacy decision (Art. 45 GDPR).
        Details are in <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact form and email</h2>
      <p>
        When you write to us through the contact form or by email, we process the details you provide: your name, email
        address, optionally your company, the topic and your message. We use them only to answer your request.
      </p>
      <p>
        If your request relates to a contract or to steps before entering one, the legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR;
        otherwise it is our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>
        Messages from the form are delivered through Cloudflare Email Routing to our mailbox, which is hosted by
        {legal.mailboxProvider}. We delete your message once your request is resolved, unless statutory retention periods,
        for example for business correspondence under German commercial and tax law, require us to keep it longer.
      </p>

      <h2>Spam protection with Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people and automated bots apart. Turnstile loads only on the
        contact page. It evaluates signals from your browser and device, including your IP address, which Cloudflare uses
        to detect abuse and not for advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is our legitimate interest in protecting the form from spam and abuse (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). The
        provider is Cloudflare, Inc., as described under Hosting and delivery.
      </p>

      {
        site.analyticsToken && (
          <>
            <h2>Web analytics</h2>
            <p>
              We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views and measure loading performance. It sets no cookies,
              stores nothing on your device and does not build profiles of individual visitors. The legal basis is our
              legitimate interest in understanding how the website is used (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
            </p>
          </>
        )
      }

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>With regard to your personal data, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
        <li>have it corrected (Art. 16 GDPR) or erased (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
        <li>restrict its processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
        <li>receive it in a portable format (Art. 20 GDPR),</li>
        <li>object to processing based on our legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>. You also have the right to
        lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We update this policy when the website or the legal requirements change. The current version is always on this page.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
